  "secure_free_lifecycle": "sc_heap_free tests the token accessibility predicate, conditionally zeroes only HLOS-accessible buffers, then returns space to gen_pool; it does not undo whole-heap SCM assignment.",
  "state_verification_limits": [
    "Heap token/is_secure and successful creation show assignment succeeded earlier, not a live hypervisor owner query.",
    "gen_pool_avail == size under the heap write semaphore proves no allocated pool ranges at that point; firmware/DMA quiescence needs separate evidence.",
    "The semaphore protects allocation/free pool operations, not all external hardware or an allocation already between unlock and export.",
    "Static heap ranges do not cover all dynamically assigned secure-system buffers; handling these two ranges alone is not a full handoff proof."
  ],
  "minimal_correct_direction": "Quiesce consumers and prevent new allocations; validate exact live heap identity, DT range, declared VMID token and empty pool; use the supported SCM/hyp assignment API with the complete verified previous VMID set to reclaim to HLOS before target CPU zeroing. Abort kexec on mismatch, in-use memory, unproven quiescence or SCM failure. Retain target zero and ordinary re-assignment. Any reuse alternative requires a defined ownership/data-lifetime handoff, not skipping memset.",
